// ATT&CK: T1562.001 — Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools
// Detects Microsoft Defender Antivirus or tamper protection being disabled
// on an endpoint — a common pre-malware-deployment step, since most
// commodity malware and ransomware fails or gets caught immediately with
// real-time protection still active.
// Data source: DeviceEvents (Defender for Endpoint advanced hunting)
//
// Schema note, stated honestly: Microsoft's advanced hunting ActionType
// values are documented but do shift between schema versions — verify
// current ActionType strings against the live Advanced Hunting schema
// reference before relying on this in production rather than assuming
// this exact list is still current.

DeviceEvents
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where ActionType in (
    "AntivirusDisabled",
    "AntivirusScanCancelled",
    "TamperingAttempt",
    "DefenderStatusChanged"
)
| project TimeGenerated, DeviceName, ActionType, InitiatingProcessAccountName,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessFileName
| extend AlertSeverity = "High"
